   "source": [
    "# Deep Hedging of a European Call Option in the Black–Scholes Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dd61e386-f037-4784-a966-d74f5aef180c",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "dd61e386-f037-4784-a966-d74f5aef180c"
   },
   "source": [
    "In this notebook I study how well neural networks can learn to hedge a European call option, and compare the learned strategies with the classical Black–Scholes delta hedge.\n",
    "\n",
    "The setup is a Black–Scholes market with zero interest rate, in which the stock price follows\n",
    "$$\n",
    "dS_t = \\sigma S_t \\, dW_t, \\qquad S_0 = s_0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "observed at $N = 30$ equally spaced times over one month. A hedging strategy $H = (H_{t_0}, \\dots, H_{t_{N-1}})$ is evaluated through the hedging loss\n",
    "$$\n",
    "g(S_T) - p(S_0) - \\sum_{j=0}^{N-1} H_{t_j} \\big( S_{t_{j+1}} - S_{t_j} \\big),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "where $g(s) = (s - K)^+$ is the call payoff and $p$ is the Black–Scholes price.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook is organised as follows:\n",
    "1. **Simulation and a first deep hedging model**: one network per time step.\n",
    "2. **The analytical Black–Scholes hedge**: derivation, evaluation and comparison with the learned strategies.\n",
    "3. **A single time-dependent network**: one network taking both price and time as input, and a comparison of all three approaches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "e2e8a728",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "e2e8a728"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
