    "# 1. Simulation and a first deep hedging model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e1793f0",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "9e1793f0"
   },
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 The Black–Scholes solution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "21d31df1",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "21d31df1"
   },
   "source": [
    "First I check that the explicit expression for $S_t$ used in the simulation indeed solves the SDE."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0305696b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We verify that $S_t = s_0 \\exp\\left( \\sigma W_t - \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 t \\right)$ is a solution to the following SDE:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "dS_t = \\sigma S_t \\, dW_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Ito's formula for a function $f (t, W_t)$ is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "dS_t = \\left( \\frac{\\partial S_t}{\\partial t} + \\tfrac{1}{2} \\frac{\\partial^2 S_t}{\\partial W_t^2} \\right) dt + \\frac{\\partial S_t}{\\partial W_t} \\, dW_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The partial derivatives of $S_t$ are given as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial S_t}{\\partial t} = s_0 e^{\\sigma W_t - \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 t} \\left( -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 \\right) = -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 S_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial S_t}{\\partial W_t} = s_0 e^{\\sigma W_t - \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 t} \\sigma = \\sigma S_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2 S_t}{\\partial W_t^2} = \\sigma \\frac{\\partial S_t}{\\partial W_t} = \\sigma (\\sigma S_t) = \\sigma^2 S_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Substituting the computed derivatives:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "dS_t = \\left( -\\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 S_t + \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 S_t \\right) dt + \\sigma S_t \\, dW_t = \\sigma S_t d W_t\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "which is the Black–Scholes SDE with $r = 0$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7b164cba",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "7b164cba"
   },
   "source": [
    "Alternatively, one can derive the solution directly by applying Itô's formula to the logarithm:\n",
    "\n",
    "For $ f\\left(S_t\\right) = \\log\\left(S_t\\right) $ we have: $ df = f^{'}\\left(S_t\\right)dS_t + \\frac{1}{2}f^{''}\\left(S_t\\right)\\left(dS_t\\right)^{2} = \\frac{1}{S_t}dS_t + \\frac{1}{2}\\left(S_t^{-2}\\right)\\left(S_t^{2}\\sigma^{2}dt\\right) = \\frac{1}{S_t}\\left(rS_tdt + \\sigma S_tdW_t\\right) - \\frac{1}{2}\\sigma^{2}dt = \\sigma dW_t + \\left(r - \\frac{\\sigma^{2}}{2}\\right)dt $ so $ \\log\\left(S_t\\right) =  \\log\\left(S_0\\right) + \\sigma W_t + \\left(r - \\frac{\\sigma^{2}}{2}\\right)t $ which implies that: $ S_t = s_0 \\exp \\left( \\sigma W_t - \\frac{1}{2} \\sigma^2 t \\right) $"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d08e3471",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "d08e3471"
   },
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Generating the dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "83b8d265",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
